WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.839 --> 00:00:16.880
Zira and the other adults looked shocked.

2
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.202
One woman took a step back from Zann, obviously a bit frightened.

3
00:00:22.123 --> 00:00:23.403
"What happened, Krub?"

4
00:00:23.904 --> 00:00:24.644
one man asked.

5
00:00:25.465 --> 00:00:26.745
Krub glared at Zann.

6
00:00:26.765 --> 00:00:31.428
"A well-liked miner disappeared around the same time Zann did.

7
00:00:32.344 --> 00:00:36.665
Everyone is saying that the strange red-haired kid must have killed him."

8
00:00:37.545 --> 00:00:38.846
Perda glanced at Zira.

9
00:00:38.866 --> 00:00:42.607
"This could be the excuse she's been waiting for to lock us up!"

10
00:00:42.967 --> 00:00:43.527
Perda thought.

11
00:00:44.247 --> 00:00:49.489
After seeing what Zira was willing to do to punish a lowly plonk farmer, Perda didn't want to

12
00:00:49.529 --> 00:00:53.750
see how creatively she might "punish" Zann—and maybe his friends too.

13
00:00:54.350 --> 00:00:55.930
Perda caught Zira smirking.

14
00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.811
But the woman quickly arranged her face into a concerned expression.

15
00:00:59.831 --> 00:01:01.412
"Oh, dear!"

16
00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:02.640
she exclaimed.

17
00:01:02.660 --> 00:01:05.801
"To think we've had a murderer in our midst!

18
00:01:06.381 --> 00:01:08.522
He certainly had us all fooled!"

19
00:01:08.542 --> 00:01:10.783
"What? I didn't kill anyone!"

20
00:01:11.223 --> 00:01:11.883
Zann cried.

21
00:01:12.423 --> 00:01:12.963
He gulped.

22
00:01:12.983 --> 00:01:15.824
"At least not on purpose!"

23
00:01:17.124 --> 00:01:20.505
A gasp went up around the room, and Perda winced.

24
00:01:20.525 --> 00:01:22.706
"Oh, Zann," she thought.

25
00:01:22.726 --> 00:01:27.007
"I know you feel guilty about that guy falling into the vortex.

26
00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.567
But it wasn't your fault!"

27
00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:30.008
"Hold on."

28
00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:32.721
Mellis stepped out from behind Krub.

29
00:01:33.081 --> 00:01:35.442
Her voice sounded shaky but determined.

30
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:41.065
"Uncle Vilkor, you can't let her lock someone up based only on what Krub is saying.

31
00:01:41.965 --> 00:01:43.406
How do you know he's telling the truth?"

32
00:01:44.386 --> 00:01:46.267
Vilkor rubbed his chin thoughtfully.

33
00:01:46.287 --> 00:01:52.409
"Hmm, the girl has a point, Zira," he said, shooting a mean look at Krub.

34
00:01:52.429 --> 00:01:55.691
"We'd better investigate the matter."

35
00:01:55.711 --> 00:01:57.972
"Fine," Zira said.

36
00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:03.341
"But while we do, it's best if we keep Zann confined for the safety of Terrica."

37
00:02:04.062 --> 00:02:05.862
She started rubbing her hands together.

38
00:02:06.302 --> 00:02:08.643
Perda couldn't let Zann be taken prisoner again.

39
00:02:09.163 --> 00:02:10.083
She grabbed his arm.

40
00:02:10.103 --> 00:02:12.324
"Get Zing," she hissed at him.

41
00:02:12.984 --> 00:02:15.725
She looked toward Mellis, but Krub stood between them.

42
00:02:15.745 --> 00:02:18.365
"Oh, no," Perda thought.

43
00:02:18.385 --> 00:02:24.767
"There's no time to get to her before Zira uses whatever spell she's concocting to capture Zann."

44
00:02:25.767 --> 00:02:27.808
She hated to leave Mellis behind again.

45
00:02:28.492 --> 00:02:30.013
But what other choice did she have?

46
00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:35.278
"I'm sorry," she thought, doing her best to send a mental message.

47
00:02:36.038 --> 00:02:38.781
"I have to get Zann out of here right now."

48
00:02:39.361 --> 00:02:43.024
Mellis didn't react, so Perda didn't know if the message had reached her.

49
00:02:43.605 --> 00:02:45.647
But she didn't have any more time to worry about it.

50
00:02:46.127 --> 00:02:47.748
Zann grabbed Zing by the tail.

51
00:02:48.729 --> 00:02:50.931
Perda rubbed her free hand against her side.

52
00:02:50.951 --> 00:02:52.773
"Ready?" she whispered.

53
00:02:53.453 --> 00:02:54.154
Zann nodded.

54
00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:56.596
Zira noticed what Perda was doing.

55
00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.241
She narrowed her eyes and raised her hands.

56
00:03:00.022 --> 00:03:01.643
Mellis let out a loud scream.

57
00:03:01.663 --> 00:03:04.004
"No! You can't do this!"

58
00:03:04.524 --> 00:03:05.545
she shrieked loudly.

59
00:03:05.565 --> 00:03:07.065
"Please, don't!"

60
00:03:07.746 --> 00:03:11.108
Zira, Vilkor, and the other adults turned to stare at her.

61
00:03:11.128 --> 00:03:13.829
"This is our chance," Perda thought.

62
00:03:13.849 --> 00:03:15.750
"Zap!" she cried.

63
00:03:17.431 --> 00:03:20.493
She, Zann, and Zing landed in a rural area.

64
00:03:20.993 --> 00:03:26.356
A few lights glowed from nearby farmhouses, and a brighter glow came from the village on the horizon.

65
00:03:27.164 --> 00:03:29.605
"Whew!" Zann said, releasing Zing.

66
00:03:29.625 --> 00:03:31.085
"That was close."

67
00:03:31.945 --> 00:03:33.426
Perda glanced toward the village.

68
00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:38.767
"I can't believe I had to leave Mellis behind again," she said, feeling miserable.

69
00:03:38.787 --> 00:03:42.888
"She seemed really scared that we were leaving without her."

70
00:03:42.908 --> 00:03:45.269
"Are you sure that's why she screamed?"

71
00:03:45.649 --> 00:03:46.289
Zann asked.

72
00:03:46.309 --> 00:03:49.690
"I thought she was trying to distract everyone so we could zap away."

73
00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:51.691
Perda blinked.

74
00:03:52.151 --> 00:03:52.971
Could Zann be right?

75
00:03:52.991 --> 00:03:58.229
"Mellis is so much braver now than she was when we arrived," she said thoughtfully.

76
00:03:58.249 --> 00:04:02.192
"It does seem strange that she'd scream out in fear like that."

77
00:04:02.973 --> 00:04:03.534
She shrugged.

78
00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.396
"Still, I wish we hadn't had to leave her."

79
00:04:06.416 --> 00:04:08.458
"Me too," Zann said.

80
00:04:08.478 --> 00:04:11.981
"But now that I'm a fugitive, we should probably keep moving."

81
00:04:12.761 --> 00:04:15.584
He whistled for Zing, and then grabbed Perda's hand.

82
00:04:15.604 --> 00:04:19.307
"Zap!" Splash!

83
00:04:20.188 --> 00:04:23.471
They landed in a cold stream in a dark, hilly area.

84
00:04:23.491 --> 00:04:24.832
"Where are we?"

85
00:04:25.292 --> 00:04:28.255
Perda asked, looking around at the unfamiliar landscape.

86
00:04:29.436 --> 00:04:33.179
Zann stepped out of the stream and magically dried his shoes and pants.

87
00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:34.880
"Sorry about that."

88
00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:36.762
He grinned sheepishly.

89
00:04:36.782 --> 00:04:38.983
"Maybe you should do the next zap.

90
00:04:39.624 --> 00:04:42.426
If we try, we might be able to reach the mines by morning."

91
00:04:43.187 --> 00:04:44.708
"You want to go to the wormhole?"

92
00:04:45.068 --> 00:04:45.589
Perda said.

93
00:04:45.609 --> 00:04:48.451
"But we can't leave Mellis behind!"

94
00:04:48.471 --> 00:04:51.994
"She told us she didn't want to leave Terrica," Zann said.

95
00:04:52.014 --> 00:04:53.876
"I doubt she's changed her mind.

96
00:04:54.508 --> 00:04:58.170
But we don't really have a choice now that everyone thinks I murdered that man."

97
00:04:58.830 --> 00:04:59.631
He looked sad.

98
00:05:00.711 --> 00:05:01.612
Perda bit her lip.

99
00:05:01.632 --> 00:05:04.393
"What if Zira takes Mellis prisoner again?"

100
00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:05.293
she thought.

101
00:05:05.313 --> 00:05:08.975
"I doubt Vilkor would lift a finger to stop Zira.

102
00:05:09.455 --> 00:05:10.356
But Zann's right.

103
00:05:11.016 --> 00:05:12.737
He's in danger if we stay."

104
00:05:13.417 --> 00:05:15.958
She sighed, staring at the rushing stream.

105
00:05:15.978 --> 00:05:18.960
"We're not safe here anymore," she said.

106
00:05:19.596 --> 00:05:24.360
"But promise me we'll tell your parents and Boz what happened here as soon as we get back

107
00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:25.541
to Magica, okay?"

108
00:05:25.561 --> 00:05:27.723
"Absolutely!" Zann said.

109
00:05:27.743 --> 00:05:30.345
"I bet they can help us figure out how to help Mellis.

110
00:05:30.705 --> 00:05:33.527
Besides, my parents will definitely want to visit this world."

111
00:05:35.189 --> 00:05:36.490
Perda slowly nodded.

112
00:05:36.510 --> 00:05:39.512
"Grab Zing again, and let's keep going."

113
00:05:41.514 --> 00:05:44.236
They reached the wormhole just as the sun rose.

114
00:05:45.216 --> 00:05:49.360
In the distance they heard the sounds of miners getting ready to start the day's work.

115
00:05:50.412 --> 00:05:52.533
"Let's not waste any time," Zann said.

116
00:05:52.553 --> 00:05:54.453
"I don't want anyone to see us."

117
00:05:55.313 --> 00:05:56.894
Perda nodded and looked around.

118
00:05:57.494 --> 00:06:01.355
Terrica was a beautiful world now that it was filling up with magic.

119
00:06:02.135 --> 00:06:07.257
The trees were lush, and birds fluttered everywhere, filling the air with their songs.

120
00:06:07.277 --> 00:06:11.278
"I'd like to come back here sometime," she said.

121
00:06:11.298 --> 00:06:15.019
"It will become even more beautiful as the magic spreads.

122
00:06:15.739 --> 00:06:18.280
Maybe your parents will let us join their expedition."

123
00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.717
"Maybe," Zann said, reaching for her hand.

124
00:06:21.737 --> 00:06:24.199
"Come on, Zing, we're going home."

125
00:06:24.759 --> 00:06:26.680
He whistled, and the dragon joined them.

126
00:06:27.521 --> 00:06:32.163
Perda created Mutual Shackles so they couldn't be accidentally separated in the vortex.

127
00:06:32.784 --> 00:06:34.465
Then she glanced at Zann.

128
00:06:35.165 --> 00:06:35.906
"Ready to go?"

129
00:06:36.366 --> 00:06:36.806
she asked.

130
00:06:37.427 --> 00:06:37.887
He nodded.

131
00:06:37.927 --> 00:06:39.248
"Let's do this."
